  "notes": "To shut one's eyes; nearly always used in the phrase {目|め}をつぶる. Occasionally written {瞑|つぶ}る.\n\nCOMMON EXPRESSIONS:\n- {目|め}をつぶる: literally \"to close one's eyes\"; also used figuratively to mean to turn a blind eye to (overlook) a fault or problem\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {閉|と}じる: to close — used for eyes, books, doors, and much else; more general and neutral\n- つぶる: specific to squeezing the eyes shut",
